WEBVTT

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:07.785
Set an Outcome only on a disposition the platform should apply on its

00:00:07.785 --> 00:00:10.841
own, when a call ends in a way nobody chose.

00:00:10.841 --> 00:00:13.470
Leave it at None for everything else.

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:18.509
Number not in service adds the called number to the Numbers Not In

00:00:18.509 --> 00:00:21.963
Service list, so it is never loaded or dialed again.

00:00:21.963 --> 00:00:26.729
No answer, Busy and Answering machine cover calls that were not picked up,

00:00:26.729 --> 00:00:29.290
by the dialer and by automated calls.

00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:34.707
Rejected and Call failed are for calls the network declined or failed.

00:00:34.707 --> 00:00:39.312
Disconnected is for a customer who hung up before an agent joined, or

00:00:39.312 --> 00:00:42.260
before an automated call decided anything.

00:00:43.010 --> 00:00:47.181
The dialer applies these to every call that ends before an agent is

00:00:47.181 --> 00:00:50.210
connected, so the agent never sees those calls.

00:00:51.816 --> 00:00:57.986
Here, a disposition named Number Not In Service gets the outcome Number not in service.

00:01:04.562 --> 00:01:08.691
A second one, named No Answer, gets the outcome No answer.

00:01:08.691 --> 00:01:12.885
The list shows each outcome as a badge next to the name, so

00:01:12.885 --> 00:01:15.982
the dialer knows which disposition to use.

